    "helpGuideStep1Title": "Set up the library",
    "helpGuideStep1Body": "Open Settings → Library profile to record the library's name, contact details and currency. Then set borrowing periods, fine rates and grace days under Loan rules - every loan and fine after that follows those numbers.",
    "helpGuideStep2Title": "Add staff accounts",
    "helpGuideStep2Body": "Everyone working the desk gets their own account under Staff, with a role that decides what they may change. A shared login makes a waived fine impossible to trace back to a person.",
    "helpGuideStep3Title": "Build the catalogue",
    "helpGuideStep3Body": "In Catalogue, create a Title for each work - author, ISBN, subject, format. Then add a Copy for every physical item on the shelf, each with its own barcode and call number. One title, many copies: that is what lets three people borrow the same book at once.",
    "helpGuideStep4Title": "Print labels and barcodes",
    "helpGuideStep4Body": "Catalogue → Labels and barcodes prints spine labels and barcode stickers for new copies, so a handheld scanner can read them at the desk instead of someone typing a call number.",
    "helpGuideStep5Title": "-Register members",
    "helpGuideStep5Body": "Members holds every borrower - student, teacher or public - with a membership type that decides how many items they may hold and for how long.",
    "helpGuideStep6Title": "Work the circulation desk",
    "helpGuideStep6Body": "Check out pairs a member with a copy and opens a loan. Return closes it and raises any overdue fine. Reservations queues a title that is already out, and Fines records what was paid or waived.",
    "helpGuideStep7Title": "Watch the numbers",
    "helpGuideStep7Body": "Dashboard shows the day at a glance. Reports goes deeper - circulation over time, overdue items, the titles that move most - and exports what you need to CSV.",
    "helpGuideStep8Title": "Back up, regularly",
    "helpGuideStep8Body": "Settings → Backup and restore writes the whole catalogue to a single file. Keep a copy somewhere other than this machine: it is the library's only record.",
